# Everything is LF in the working tree on every platform, so shell scripts and
# Go sources are byte-identical wherever they are checked out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixture contexts and golden files are data whose exact bytes are asserted: a
# walk reports each file's size and the goldens record the totals. Git's
# autocrlf adds a byte per line on Windows, which changed those totals and
# failed every golden test there. Later patterns win, so this overrides the
# rule above.
testdata/** -text
